#ASSERT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 1995 provident-fund employee, as the law asks` `an engineer of the State in 1995`)

§§ `3 קופת גמל ופנסיה צוברת`

-- ¶1: a provident fund for benefits ("קופת גמל לתגמולים") as the Income Tax
-- (Rules for Approving and Running Provident Funds) Regulations, 1964,
-- mean it, as the unions choose with the employers' written consent;
-- ¶2: an accrual pension is one in a comprehensive pension fund.
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p2
DECLARE `fund of 10.8.1995` IS ONE OF
    `a provident fund for benefits, of 10.8.1995`
    `an accrual pension in a comprehensive fund, of 10.8.1995`

`the fund the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 pays into` MEANS `a provident fund for benefits, of 10.8.1995`

`why the provident-fund regulations are not in the agreement of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "תקנות מס הכנסה (כללים לאישור ולניהול קופות גמל), התשכ\"ד-1964"

GIVEN `the employers consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a union's choice of fund stands under 10.8.1995` `the employers consented in writing` IF
    `the employers consented in writing`

§§ `4–5 הסדר הביניים`

-- §4: until the legislation (§11) and the accrual pension on those
-- components, the parties agree the interim arrangement of §5 for the
-- employees it covers. §5: from 1.1.95 the employers transfer to a
-- provident fund, for every such employee, as follows.
@desc A payment, as the agreement of 10.8.1995 and its annexes tell them apart.
DECLARE `1995 payment` IS ONE OF
    `overtime, of 10.8.1995`
    `extra work, standbys, duty shifts and shifts, of 10.8.1995`
    `premiums, of 10.8.1995`
    `fixed and variable car expenses, of 10.8.1995`
    `travel expenses, of 10.8.1995`
    `subsistence, of 10.8.1995`
    `compulsory insurance, of 10.8.1995`
    `comprehensive insurance, of 10.8.1995`
    `car licence fees, of 10.8.1995`
    `a tax gross-up, of 10.8.1995`
    `another payment that is not pensionable, of 10.8.1995`
    `a pensionable payment, of 10.8.1995`

-- Annex ב': from 1.1.95, 5% and 5% on (א) overtime, (ב) extra work —
-- standbys, duty shifts, shifts and any payment for other extra work —
-- (ג) premiums, (ד) fixed and variable car expenses, (ה) travel expenses,
-- (ו) subsistence, each in full in the month it is paid.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_a akn:att_2__hc_1__para_b akn:att_2__hc_1__para_c akn:att_2__hc_1__para_d akn:att_2__hc_1__para_e akn:att_2__hc_1__para_f
`the components of annex ב' of 1995` MEANS
    LIST `overtime, of 10.8.1995`, `extra work, standbys, duty shifts and shifts, of 10.8.1995`, `premiums, of 10.8.1995`,
         `fixed and variable car expenses, of 10.8.1995`, `travel expenses, of 10.8.1995`, `subsistence, of 10.8.1995`

-- Annex ג': from 1.1.96, annex ב''s and (א) compulsory insurance, (ב)
-- comprehensive insurance, (ג) car licence fees.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_a akn:att_3__hc_1__para_b akn:att_3__hc_1__para_c
`the components of annex ג' of 1995` MEANS
    append `the components of annex ב' of 1995`
           (LIST `compulsory insurance, of 10.8.1995`, `comprehensive insurance, of 10.8.1995`, `car licence fees, of 10.8.1995`)

-- Annex ד': from 1.6.97, annexes ב' and ג''s and every other component and
-- payment that is not pensionable — wage supplements, supplements that are
-- not wage and other refunds among them — save the tax gross-up, and
-- subject to §3 of annex ו' (a component new in substance comes in within
-- the cost frame).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/p1
GIVEN p IS A `1995 payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `annex ד' of 1995 brings in` p IF
    NOT (p EQUALS `a pensionable payment, of 10.8.1995` OR p EQUALS `a tax gross-up, of 10.8.1995`)

-- §5(א)(1): from 1.1.1995 the employer contributes 5% and deducts 5%, every
-- month, on the components of annex ב'; (ב) from 1.1.1996, of annex ג';
-- (ג) from 1.6.1997, of annex ד'. (ה): no contribution on a tax gross-up.
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_5 akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_5__para_b akn:art_5__para_c akn:art_5__para_e
`the employer's provident-fund contribution of 10.8.1995` MEANS 5%
`the employee's provident-fund deduction of 10.8.1995` MEANS 5%

`the steps of the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1996, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997

GIVEN d IS A DATE, p IS A `1995 payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` d p IF
        (    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997)
         AND `annex ד' of 1995 brings in` p)
    OR  (    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1996)
         AND elem p `the components of annex ג' of 1995`)
    OR  (    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995)
         AND elem p `the components of annex ב' of 1995`)

@desc The provident-fund contribution and deduction on a payment, under the agreement of 10.8.1995.
DECLARE `1995 provident-fund amounts` HAS
    `the employer's contribution of 10.8.1995` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's deduction of 10.8.1995`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN d IS A DATE, p IS A `1995 payment`, amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `1995 provident-fund amounts`
DECIDE `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on` d p amount IS
    IF `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` d p
    THEN JUST (`1995 provident-fund amounts` WITH
                  `the employer's contribution of 10.8.1995` IS `the employer's provident-fund contribution of 10.8.1995` TIMES amount
                  `the employee's deduction of 10.8.1995`    IS `the employee's provident-fund deduction of 10.8.1995` TIMES amount)
    ELSE NOTHING

`contributing under the agreement of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `contribute and deduct 5% each to a provident fund under the agreement of 10.8.1995`

-- (א)(1) ¶2: the retroactive contribution, for every month from 1.1.95 to
-- the start in fact, is made in the first salary after the unions choose
-- the funds with the employers' consent ("מועד תחילת ההפרשה בפועל", for
-- §8); (א)(2): from then the contribution is current, every month, by
-- (א)–(ג) and annexes ב'–ד'.
@ref akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_2
`making the retroactive contribution of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `make the retroactive contribution of 10.8.1995 in the first salary after the funds are chosen`

GIVEN `the start in fact` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months of the retroactive contribution of 10.8.1995` `the start in fact` IS
    (DATE_YEAR `the start in fact` MINUS 1995) TIMES 12 PLUS DATE_MONTH `the start in fact` MINUS 1

-- (ד): where the employee is not entitled to a component, nothing is
-- contributed or deducted on it while he is not; and the agreement does
-- not on its own oblige the employer to pay any further component.
@ref akn:art_5__para_d
`the 1995 provident-fund amounts on a component he is not paid` MEANS
    `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1996) `overtime, of 10.8.1995` 0

`the agreement of 10.8.1995 obliges paying further components` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on a component he is not paid` EQUALS JUST (`1995 provident-fund amounts` 0 0)

-- An overtime payment of 1,000 in February 1995: 50 and 50. Car insurance:
-- nothing in 1995, 50 and 50 from January 1996. Any other component that is
-- not pensionable: nothing before June 1997. A tax gross-up: never.
#ASSERT `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 1995) `overtime, of 10.8.1995` 1000 EQUALS JUST (`1995 provident-fund amounts` 50 50)
#ASSERT `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 1995) `comprehensive insurance, of 10.8.1995` 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the 1995 provident-fund amounts on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1996) `comprehensive insurance, of 10.8.1995` 1000 EQUALS JUST (`1995 provident-fund amounts` 50 50)
#ASSERT NOT `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1997) `another payment that is not pensionable, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997) `another payment that is not pensionable, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT NOT `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997) `a tax gross-up, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT NOT `the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995 contributes on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997) `a pensionable payment, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT `the months of the retroactive contribution of 10.8.1995` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 1995) EQUALS 10

§§ `6–7 הזכאות לכספים והמחלוקת על "עמיתים ותיקים"`

-- §6: the employee is entitled, when his employment ends and in any other
-- case usual for a provident fund, to all the sums gathered to his credit,
-- on the terms that entitle to benefits under those regulations.
-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: §6 names the end of the employment
-- relation only as when the employee may draw what accrued in the
-- provident fund; it gives or asks no notice, so it rules nothing the law
-- puts a floor under.
@ref akn:art_6
`the employee is entitled to all the sums gathered under 10.8.1995` MEANS TRUE

-- Annex ה': ¶1 the new accrual-pension funds' arrangement of January 1995
-- changed the accrual table and the government's support of the bonds'
-- interest; ¶2–¶3 the Histadrut demands that, when the interim arrangement
-- ends, the employees be recognised in the funds as "veteran members", or
-- compensated; ¶4 the government and the employers refuse both, holding
-- the cost of this agreement full compensation; ¶5 the Histadrut holds it
-- no compensation for that at all; ¶6 while the dispute stands the
-- Histadrut and the unions may act by §7. §7: while it stands, the
-- Histadrut and the unions have the right to stay in the interim
-- arrangement, and not move to an accrual pension, for all the employees.
@ref akn:art_7 akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1/p6
GIVEN `the veteran-members dispute is settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unions may stay in the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995` `the veteran-members dispute is settled` IF
    NOT `the veteran-members dispute is settled`

#ASSERT `the unions may stay in the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995` FALSE

§§ `8 פיצוי לגמלאים`

-- (א): a retiree who left an employer the agreement covers between 1.1.93
-- and the start in fact, and for whom nothing was contributed under the
-- wage agreements or this one because of when he left, is compensated by a
-- one-time payment: (1) 0.5% of his salary determining the pension in the
-- month of payment for each month of 1993; (2) 1% for each month of 1994;
-- (3) 1.5% for each month from 1.1.95 to the start in fact. (ב): paid at
-- the start in fact, for the time from 1.1.93 to his retirement.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_8__para_b
`the 1995 compensation for a month of 1993` MEANS 0.5%
`the 1995 compensation for a month of 1994` MEANS 1%
`the 1995 compensation for a month from 1995` MEANS 1.5%

GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `the start in fact` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a retiree compensated under 10.8.1995` `retired on` `the start in fact` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1993)
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` `the start in fact`

GIVEN `months in 1993` IS A NUMBER
      `months in 1994` IS A NUMBER
      `months from 1995` IS A NUMBER
      `his pension salary in the month of payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1995 one-time compensation of a retiree` `months in 1993` `months in 1994` `months from 1995` `his pension salary in the month of payment` IS
    `the 1995 compensation's share of the pension salary` `months in 1993` `months in 1994` `months from 1995` TIMES `his pension salary in the month of payment`

GIVEN `months in 1993` IS A NUMBER
      `months in 1994` IS A NUMBER
      `months from 1995` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1995 compensation's share of the pension salary` `months in 1993` `months in 1994` `months from 1995` IS
    sum (LIST `months in 1993` TIMES `the 1995 compensation for a month of 1993`,
              `months in 1994` TIMES `the 1995 compensation for a month of 1994`,
              `months from 1995` TIMES `the 1995 compensation for a month from 1995`)

`paying the retiree's compensation of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the one-time compensation of 10.8.1995 to a retiree`

-- One who retired at the end of June 1995, his pension salary 5,000 in
-- the month of payment: 12 × 0.5% + 12 × 1% + 6 × 1.5% = 27%, 1,350.
#ASSERT `the 1995 compensation's share of the pension salary` 12 12 6 EQUALS 27%
#ASSERT `the 1995 one-time compensation of a retiree` 12 12 6 5000 EQUALS 1350
#ASSERT `a retiree compensated under 10.8.1995` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 1995) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 1995)
#ASSERT NOT `a retiree compensated under 10.8.1995` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 1992) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 1995)

§§ `9–10 בלי כפל ובלי הרחבה`

-- §9: where on the signing day contributions to a pension or a provident
-- fund are made on a component, none is made on it again under this one.
@ref akn:art_9
GIVEN `contributions are made on it on the signing day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 10.8.1995 contributes on the component` `contributions are made on it on the signing day` IF
    NOT `contributions are made on it on the signing day`

#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 10.8.1995 contributes on the component` TRUE

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §10 says only that the
-- agreement does not of itself put the non-pension components it
-- contributes on into the wage severance is computed on; which components
-- count, §13 sends to the regulations, and the agreement gives or takes
-- nothing there.

-- §10: the agreement does not on its own oblige contributions on those
-- components to other funds (training funds, knowledge funds), nor
-- recognise them for a pension by law, severance pay or the hour value.
@ref akn:art_10
DECLARE `what the 1995 components do not thereby count for` IS ONE OF
    `other funds, training and knowledge funds among them, of 10.8.1995`
    `a pension by law, of 10.8.1995`
    `severance pay, of 10.8.1995`
    `the hour value, of 10.8.1995`

GIVEN p IS A `what the 1995 components do not thereby count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 10.8.1995 on its own makes the components count for` p IF FALSE

§§ `11 החקיקה וסיום הסדר הביניים`

-- (א): the Treasury submits at once a bill amending the State Service
-- (Pensions) Law, and any other law needed, to let those components carry
-- an accrual pension for an employee on a budgetary pension; (ב): drafted
-- with the Histadrut's agreement, and any regulations made in cooperation
-- with it.
@ref akn:art_11__para_a akn:art_11__para_b
`submitting the bill of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `submit the bill amending the State Service (Pensions) Law under the agreement of 10.8.1995`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Treasury`
           MUST  `draft the bill of 10.8.1995 with the Histadrut's agreement`)

`the Treasury's regulations of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `cooperate with the Histadrut on the regulations of 10.8.1995`

-- (ג): when the legislation ends and contributions to an accrual pension
-- begin on the components contributed on here, the provident-fund
-- contributions on them stop; ¶2: subject to §§7 and 13.
@ref akn:art_11__para_c akn:art_11__para_c/p2
GIVEN `accrual-pension contributions began on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unions stay in the interim arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `fund of 10.8.1995`
DECIDE `where a component's contributions go under 10.8.1995` `accrual-pension contributions began on it` `the unions stay in the interim arrangement` IS
    IF `accrual-pension contributions began on it` AND NOT `the unions stay in the interim arrangement`
    THEN `an accrual pension in a comprehensive fund, of 10.8.1995`
    ELSE `a provident fund for benefits, of 10.8.1995`

#ASSERT `where a component's contributions go under 10.8.1995` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a provident fund for benefits, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT `where a component's contributions go under 10.8.1995` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an accrual pension in a comprehensive fund, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT `where a component's contributions go under 10.8.1995` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a provident fund for benefits, of 10.8.1995`

-- (ד): where the law allows and the unions ask, the deposits move from the
-- provident fund to the accrual pension fund, seniority in the one counted
-- in the other.
@ref akn:art_11__para_d
GIVEN `the law allows it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the unions ask` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposits of 10.8.1995 move to the accrual fund` `the law allows it` `the unions ask` IF
    `the law allows it` AND `the unions ask`

-- (ה): the Histadrut's position, that the wage agreements can be carried
-- out with no legislation; ¶2: the employers', that an accrual pension for
-- one entitled to a budgetary pension needs the amendment. Positions, no
-- rule.
@ref akn:art_11__para_e akn:art_11__para_e/p2
`the Histadrut holds no legislation is needed, under 10.8.1995` MEANS TRUE
`the employers hold the amendment is needed, under 10.8.1995` MEANS TRUE

§§ `12 הסכמי השכר`

-- ¶1: the wage agreements' provisions on the accrual pension stand, and in
-- the time contributions are made here, this agreement applies. ¶2: the
-- unions that signed it, and the Histadrut for them, have no claim to a
-- retroactive contribution under the wage agreements for that time.
@ref akn:art_12 akn:art_12/p2
GIVEN `contributions are made under the interim arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `what governs the accrual pension under 10.8.1995` `contributions are made under the interim arrangement` IS
    IF `contributions are made under the interim arrangement`
    THEN "ההסכם מיום 10.8.1995"
    ELSE "ההוראות בהסכמי השכר"

`no retroactive claim for the interim period, of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `claim a retroactive contribution under the wage agreements for the interim period`

§§ `13 בחירת האיגודים בסיום הסדר הביניים`

-- When the interim arrangement ends and the accrual pension begins, a
-- union that signed may decide: (א) for its employees with less than ten
-- years to their pension on that day, that they stay in the interim
-- arrangement; (ב) for those with more than ten, that they stay in a
-- provident fund rather than the pension, adjusted to that union's wage
-- agreement. Ten years exactly is neither "less" nor "more" (convention
-- thresholds.above): §13 gives the union no choice for them
-- (F-framework-1995-b), so they move by §11(ג).
@ref akn:art_13 akn:art_13__para_a akn:art_13__para_b
DECLARE `the union's choice at the end of 10.8.1995` IS ONE OF
    `stay in the interim arrangement, of 10.8.1995`
    `stay in a provident fund adjusted to the wage agreement, of 10.8.1995`
    `no choice under §13, of 10.8.1995`

GIVEN `years of work left to his pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `the union's choice at the end of 10.8.1995`
DECIDE `the choice §13 of 10.8.1995 gives the union for` `years of work left to his pension` IS
    IF `years of work left to his pension` LESS THAN 10
    THEN `stay in the interim arrangement, of 10.8.1995`
    ELSE IF `years of work left to his pension` `is above` 10
         THEN `stay in a provident fund adjusted to the wage agreement, of 10.8.1995`
         ELSE `no choice under §13, of 10.8.1995`

`why §13 of 10.8.1995 gives no choice at ten years` MEANS `the text is silent` "F-framework-1995-b"

`§13 of 10.8.1995 leaves exactly ten years out` MEANS
    `the choice §13 of 10.8.1995 gives the union for` 10 EQUALS `no choice under §13, of 10.8.1995`

#ASSERT `§13 of 10.8.1995 leaves exactly ten years out`
#ASSERT `the choice §13 of 10.8.1995 gives the union for` 9.5 EQUALS `stay in the interim arrangement, of 10.8.1995`
#ASSERT `the choice §13 of 10.8.1995 gives the union for` 12 EQUALS `stay in a provident fund adjusted to the wage agreement, of 10.8.1995`

§§ `14–16 הסדר שונה, תנאים קודמים ורישום`

-- §14: if in the agreement's time another union is given a different
-- arrangement on those components, a union that signed may choose to join
-- it instead of this one, or to bring this one's terms to it.
@ref akn:art_14
GIVEN `another union was given a different arrangement in the agreement's time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a union of 10.8.1995 may join or match another arrangement` `another union was given a different arrangement in the agreement's time` IF
    `another union was given a different arrangement in the agreement's time`

-- §15: terms the parties set before in collective agreements, arrangements
-- or undertakings stay in force, unless this one amends or cancels them.
@ref akn:art_15
GIVEN `this agreement amends or cancels it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stays in force under 10.8.1995` `this agreement amends or cancels it` IF
    NOT `this agreement amends or cancels it`

-- §16: submitted for registration as a collective agreement on signing.
@ref akn:art_16
`registering the agreement of 10.8.1995` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `submit the agreement of 10.8.1995 for registration`

§§ `נספח ו' — עלויות`

-- ¶1: the cost frame of the interim arrangement, as computed on signing:
-- 1(א) an average 2.15% to the employer of the salary determining the
-- pension of all its employees in annex א''s scales (one average over all
-- of them, not one a scale — "השכר הקובע לפנסיה"), for the employer's 5%
-- on annex ב'; (ב) 2.5% for annex ג'; (ג) 3% for annex ד'.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1/p1 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_6__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_6__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997) THEN 3%
    ELSE IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1996) THEN 2.5%
         ELSE IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995) THEN 2.15%
              ELSE 0

-- 2: annexes ב'–ד' were prepared on that cost, computed on the pension
-- salary of the first six months of 1995; ¶2–¶3: no reckoning between the
-- parties for any later change in the data (the employees, how many are
-- paid a component, its amount), even where the cost changes.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_2/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_2/p3
`the cost of 10.8.1995 is reckoned again for a change in the data` MEANS FALSE

-- 3(א): a component new in substance added after the signing that is not
-- pensionable is brought in, provided the average cost of the new and the
-- existing together is no more than 1's frame on its day; ¶3: all data at
-- the first half of 1995's prices; ¶4: computed jointly. (ב): a new
-- component is one no employee of the employer was paid or entitled to on
-- the signing day. (ג): the parties may still agree pensionable supplements.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_6__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the average cost of the existing components` IS A NUMBER
      `the average cost of the new component` IS A NUMBER
      `no employee was paid or entitled to it on the signing day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new component is brought in under 10.8.1995` d `the average cost of the existing components` `the average cost of the new component` `no employee was paid or entitled to it on the signing day` IF
        `no employee was paid or entitled to it on the signing day`
    AND `the average cost of the existing components` PLUS `the average cost of the new component` AT MOST `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` d

`the parties of 10.8.1995 may still agree pensionable supplements` MEANS TRUE

-- 4: the accrual pension's cost frame under the wage agreements (1993–
-- 1996) is 2% of the pension salary. 5: the annex takes nothing from the
-- agreement and the wage agreements, the parties' duties under them, or
-- whom they apply to.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_5
`the wage agreements' accrual-pension cost frame, by 10.8.1995` MEANS 2%

#ASSERT `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1995) EQUALS 2.15%
#ASSERT `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1996) EQUALS 2.5%
#ASSERT `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1997) EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `a new component is brought in under 10.8.1995` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998) (2.8%) (0.2%) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a new component is brought in under 10.8.1995` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998) (2.9%) (0.2%) TRUE
-- Every step of the interim arrangement costs more than the wage
-- agreements' frame for the accrual pension.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the cost frame of 10.8.1995 on` d GREATER THAN `the wage agreements' accrual-pension cost frame, by 10.8.1995`) `the steps of the interim arrangement of 10.8.1995`
